{
  "paper_id": "P004047",
  "units": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "A0",
      "span": "Morphology-aware statistical machine translation based on morphs induced in an unsupervised manner",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A1",
      "span": "In SMT, words are traditionally used as the smallest units of translation.",
      "roles": ["problem"],
      "origin": "prior"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A2",
      "span": "Such a system generalizes poorly to word forms that do not occur in the training data.",
      "roles": ["problem"],
      "origin": "prior"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A3",
      "span": "In particular, this is problematic for languages that are highly compounding, highly inflecting, or both.",
      "roles": ["problem"],
      "origin": "prior"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A4",
      "span": "An alternative way is to use sub-word units, such as morphemes.",
      "roles": ["task"],
      "origin": "prior"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A5",
      "span": "We use the Morfessor algorithm to find statistical morphemelike units (called morphs) that can be used to reduce the size of the lexicon and improve the ability to generalize.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A6",
      "span": "Translation and language models are trained directly on morphs instead of words.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A7",
      "span": "The approach is tested on three Nordic languages (Danish, Finnish, and Swedish) that are included in the Europarl corpus consisting of the Proceedings of the European Parliament.",
      "roles": ["dataset"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A8",
      "span": "However, in our experiments we did not obtain higher BLEU scores for the morph model than for the standard word-based approach.",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A9",
      "span": "Nonetheless, the proposed morph-based solution has clear benefits, as morphologically well motivated structures (phrases) are learned, and the proportion of words left untranslated is clearly reduced.",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    }
  ]
}

